{"id": "swebq0004", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Cuban Re bellion of 186 8 was caused by a combination of economic hardship, political repression, and racial tension. Cuba had been suffering under Spanish colonial rule for centuries, with many people living in poverty and facing harsh treatment from the authorities. When a slave uprising occurred in 1 8 5 0, it led to increased repression against the Cre olo population. Then, when a group of Cri olos rebel led in 18 6 8, they were met with brutal force from the Spanish government. This led to widespread outrage and eventually resulted in a full-scale rebellion that lasted for years before finally being put down in 1 8 78. So, while there were many factors involved, the main causes were economic hardship and political rep ression.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 38, "carrier_ended": null}
