{"id": "swebq0140", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Roman Catholic Church is a Christian church that believes in the Holy Trinity, which is God the Father, God the So n, and God the Holy Spirit. They also believe that Jesus Christ was both human and divine, and they teach that salvation comes through faith in Jesus Christ. They have many important beliefs about sacraments like baptism and con firmation, as well as the Eucharist, where bread and wine are believed to become the body and blood of Christ during mass.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
